1
00:00:00,945 --> 00:00:01,945
Yes.

2
00:00:01,945 --> 00:00:02,975
(Episode 76)

3
00:00:03,045 --> 00:00:04,845
Jeongbin Police Station, Traffic Investigation Unit?

4
00:00:06,453 --> 00:00:08,953
What? You found it?

5
00:00:14,223 --> 00:00:15,233
Honey.

6
00:00:15,893 --> 00:00:16,993
My gosh.

7
00:00:24,773 --> 00:00:26,773
(My Happy Funeral)

8
00:00:26,843 --> 00:00:27,843
What is wrong with you?

9
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:29,613
You should humor my father on a day like today.

10
00:00:29,673 --> 00:00:30,673
Go on already.

11
00:00:31,883 --> 00:00:33,843
Why are you two acting like this? It's a special day.

12
00:00:44,993 --> 00:00:46,293
Dad.

13
00:01:11,383 --> 00:01:12,383
Hey, Gyeol.

14
00:01:13,453 --> 00:01:14,453
Hey, Ko Gyeol.

15
00:01:15,123 --> 00:01:16,553
Hey, this is a once-in-a-lifetime look for Grandfather.

16
00:01:16,623 --> 00:01:17,823
Aren't you going to take a picture? Hurry up.

17
00:01:18,293 --> 00:01:20,193
- Oh, yes. - Go on, take it.

18
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:29,703
You look very tired. Why don't you go inside...

19
00:01:29,773 --> 00:01:30,773
and get some rest?

20
00:01:31,103 --> 00:01:32,773
No, I'm fine.

21
00:01:33,543 --> 00:01:34,703
Go check on the Chairman.

22
00:01:37,543 --> 00:01:40,243
- Oh my. Oh, this won't do. - Grandfather.

23
00:01:40,313 --> 00:01:41,313
Father.

24
00:01:41,653 --> 00:01:43,583
- Oh, let's go inside now. - Father.

25
00:01:43,883 --> 00:01:44,883
Chairman.

26
00:01:45,153 --> 00:01:46,183
- Chairman. - Father.

27
00:01:47,883 --> 00:01:48,893
Grandfather.

28
00:01:50,593 --> 00:01:52,293
I'm going to head inside now.

29
00:01:53,323 --> 00:01:55,533
Please enjoy yourselves before you go.

30
00:01:57,363 --> 00:02:01,133
Thank you for accepting my invitation.

31
00:02:05,043 --> 00:02:06,043
Here.

32
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:10,013
- Careful, careful. - All right, that's all for today.

33
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:11,213
Okay.

34
00:02:12,743 --> 00:02:14,213
- Move aside. - Oh my.

35
00:02:14,283 --> 00:02:16,783
Father, the sun is harsh, isn't it? Yes, be very careful, Father.

36
00:02:17,113 --> 00:02:19,783
- I'm going inside. Please clean up. - Okay.

37
00:02:22,223 --> 00:02:24,893
Leave the rest to us, and you two should head inside.

38
00:02:24,893 --> 00:02:26,993
No, it's fine. We can clean up together.

39
00:02:27,363 --> 00:02:29,093
Sorry, but I have to leave first.

40
00:02:29,363 --> 00:02:31,433
Please tell the Chairman I'm sorry I couldn't say goodbye.

41
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:34,263
- Okay. Go home and rest. - Yes.

42
00:02:35,073 --> 00:02:37,533
- Honey, what's wrong? - Dad, are you okay?

43
00:02:37,673 --> 00:02:39,143
What's wrong, Dad? Are you hurt?

44
00:02:39,403 --> 00:02:40,403
No, it's nothing like that.

45
00:02:40,703 --> 00:02:41,773
Goodbye, Chief Seo.

46
00:02:42,473 --> 00:02:44,443
Good work, Team Leader Ko.

47
00:02:45,243 --> 00:02:48,653
- You too, General Director Ko. - Sorry. We'll leave first.

48
00:02:48,713 --> 00:02:49,753
Honey, wait for me.

49
00:02:51,653 --> 00:02:54,853
What was that? That's strange.

50
00:02:55,553 --> 00:02:59,663
What's so strange that you're looking so puzzled?

51
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:02,063
It's nothing.

52
00:03:03,193 --> 00:03:06,433
Oh, I just hope the Chairman stays healthy.

53
00:03:07,503 --> 00:03:10,133
- Grandfather will be okay, right? - Let's clean up and go inside.

54
00:03:10,573 --> 00:03:11,773
Let's finish up here for today.

55
00:03:11,843 --> 00:03:14,903
- Okay. Let's all clean up. - Okay.

56
00:03:14,973 --> 00:03:16,013
Well, shall we go?

57
00:03:17,713 --> 00:03:20,143
What was that call about? You looked upset.

58
00:03:20,643 --> 00:03:22,653
It was from the police station. We'll talk later.

59
00:03:22,753 --> 00:03:24,153
Okay, I get it.

60
00:03:29,493 --> 00:03:32,163
So, how is Father?

61
00:03:32,623 --> 00:03:33,623
Well...

62
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:36,733
He just fell asleep.

63
00:03:37,733 --> 00:03:39,463
I think he overdid it today.

64
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:42,133
Gosh, I know. Why did he have to insist on...

65
00:03:42,203 --> 00:03:43,233
a living funeral?

66
00:03:44,603 --> 00:03:47,043
And Mother, you should have tried to talk him out of it.

67
00:03:47,403 --> 00:03:49,513
How could you just go along with it?

68
00:03:51,443 --> 00:03:55,313
The Chairman was adamant, and it was a very meaningful event.

69
00:03:55,313 --> 00:03:58,113
Why are you taking it out on your mother?

70
00:03:58,183 --> 00:04:00,223
Oh my, Kang Yeon Ja.

71
00:04:00,683 --> 00:04:02,493
Are you arguing with my husband right now?

72
00:04:02,893 --> 00:04:05,423
I know you're her daughter, but that's out of line.

73
00:04:05,963 --> 00:04:07,463
People should know their place. Honestly.

74
00:04:07,523 --> 00:04:09,733
Everyone, quiet down. You'll wake him.

75
00:04:12,233 --> 00:04:15,773
He said he has something to say when he wakes up,

76
00:04:16,573 --> 00:04:18,373
so wait and have dinner before you go.

77
00:04:19,073 --> 00:04:20,173
Something to say?

78
00:04:23,743 --> 00:04:27,083
Oh, honey. Isn't this ridiculous?

79
00:04:27,343 --> 00:04:29,883
Acting as if she's so important.

80
00:04:29,953 --> 00:04:32,683
She was glued to Father's side during the entire event. Honestly.

81
00:04:33,923 --> 00:04:35,323
By the way, about Father...

82
00:04:35,923 --> 00:04:37,353
Something bad isn't going to happen to him, is it?

83
00:04:37,653 --> 00:04:39,063
No way.

84
00:04:39,723 --> 00:04:41,833
But what's with Chief Seo's expression...

85
00:04:41,893 --> 00:04:42,893
the whole time?

86
00:04:43,193 --> 00:04:44,463
Did you two get in a fight or something?

87
00:04:45,203 --> 00:04:47,833
A fight? Who does he think he is to fight with me?

88
00:04:47,903 --> 00:04:50,303
Oh, sorry. I momentarily forgot...

89
00:04:50,703 --> 00:04:53,343
that you're the future head of Gangsu Group.

90
00:04:56,943 --> 00:04:58,143
Are you still not feeling well?

91
00:04:59,513 --> 00:05:01,583
I'm fine now, so don't worry.

92
00:05:02,283 --> 00:05:03,283
Why the study again?

93
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:05,253
Go to the bedroom and get some sleep.

94
00:05:05,853 --> 00:05:07,423
You're as pale as a sheet.

95
00:05:07,923 --> 00:05:10,023
What on earth is wrong with you these days? Why?

96
00:05:13,593 --> 00:05:15,133
Gosh, seriously.

97
00:05:18,903 --> 00:05:20,733
So you're saying all the records at the police station...

98
00:05:20,803 --> 00:05:21,933
with jurisdiction were destroyed?

99
00:05:22,373 --> 00:05:23,373
Yes.

100
00:05:23,773 --> 00:05:26,103
Apparently, local police stations usually get rid of...

101
00:05:26,173 --> 00:05:28,103
traffic accident records after seven years.

102
00:05:28,173 --> 00:05:30,673
Then what do we do? Is there really no other way?

103
00:05:30,773 --> 00:05:33,413
No. I've already filed an information disclosure request...

104
00:05:33,483 --> 00:05:34,483
with the police.

105
00:05:35,013 --> 00:05:36,883
Separately, I'm going to look for files...

106
00:05:36,953 --> 00:05:37,983
at the prosecutor's office.

107
00:05:38,583 --> 00:05:40,153
I'm planning to go in person on Monday.

108
00:05:40,323 --> 00:05:42,023
Oh, what a huge relief.

109
00:05:42,593 --> 00:05:45,363
After you got off the phone, you looked so upset,

110
00:05:45,623 --> 00:05:47,793
I got scared that something was wrong.

111
00:05:48,463 --> 00:05:49,463
Actually...

112
00:05:49,763 --> 00:05:50,893
Just for a moment there,

113
00:05:51,963 --> 00:05:53,563
a memory came back to me.

114
00:05:54,103 --> 00:05:55,273
What memory?

115
00:05:56,633 --> 00:05:57,973
At the scene of the accident,

116
00:05:59,143 --> 00:06:00,673
I think there were people there.

117
00:06:01,003 --> 00:06:03,513
People? Who were those people?

118
00:06:04,373 --> 00:06:05,383
I don't know.

119
00:06:06,043 --> 00:06:07,913
The memory is too hazy.

120
00:06:08,583 --> 00:06:09,913
I heard sirens,

121
00:06:10,583 --> 00:06:13,623
and I think people were standing at a distance.

122
00:06:14,253 --> 00:06:16,523
Could it have been the driver who caused the accident...

123
00:06:16,523 --> 00:06:18,963
or the police? Or paramedics?

124
00:06:19,793 --> 00:06:21,893
I don't know. It's too faint.

125
00:06:22,893 --> 00:06:24,633
Every time a memory like this comes back,

126
00:06:24,693 --> 00:06:26,603
my head hurts like it's going to split open.

127
00:06:30,503 --> 00:06:31,633
That must be so hard.

128
00:06:34,773 --> 00:06:35,913
It is, but...

129
00:06:37,213 --> 00:06:38,643
whenever a memory surfaces,

130
00:06:39,443 --> 00:06:43,553
I feel this strong urge to find out exactly what happened that day...

131
00:06:44,313 --> 00:06:45,923
and who those people were.

132
00:07:01,033 --> 00:07:02,133
It's okay.

133
00:07:02,873 --> 00:07:04,503
Everything is going to be okay.

134
00:07:09,513 --> 00:07:10,713
Do you want to get some sleep?

135
00:07:11,273 --> 00:07:13,643
It doesn't look like you slept well last night either.

136
00:07:14,943 --> 00:07:15,953
I don't want to.

137
00:07:16,683 --> 00:07:17,813
If I fall asleep,

138
00:07:18,513 --> 00:07:20,623
I'm afraid you'll go away somewhere.

139
00:07:21,683 --> 00:07:23,453
Where would I go?

140
00:07:23,993 --> 00:07:26,493
I promised I'd always be by your side, Team Leader Ko.

141
00:07:27,693 --> 00:07:30,933
Here, lie down. I'll sing you a lullaby.

142
00:07:37,603 --> 00:07:43,073
On my mother's path

143
00:07:43,573 --> 00:07:46,983
White wild roses bloom

144
00:07:48,313 --> 00:07:53,183
- The petals of the white wild rose - Is Great-grandfather very sick?

145
00:07:53,523 --> 00:07:56,293
He'll be fine soon. Don't worry too much.

146
00:07:56,793 --> 00:07:59,223
Wasn't today really touching, Eun Hyung?

147
00:07:59,523 --> 00:08:00,523
It was.

148
00:08:01,293 --> 00:08:04,163
Today's funeral didn't draw a line between life and death,

149
00:08:04,933 --> 00:08:07,533
but felt more like a celebration of that grandfather's life itself,

150
00:08:07,963 --> 00:08:09,403
so it was really meaningful. Yes.

151
00:08:10,003 --> 00:08:11,203
Oh, this.

152
00:08:11,273 --> 00:08:12,403
(Our Happy Days Real Estate, Grandma Pancake)

153
00:08:13,073 --> 00:08:16,543
Eun Hyung, did you bring this flower for me?

154
00:08:16,943 --> 00:08:19,583
Not exactly. I was clearing the table,

155
00:08:19,583 --> 00:08:21,513
and I didn't want them to be thrown out.

156
00:08:23,613 --> 00:08:24,683
Thanks.

157
00:08:29,193 --> 00:08:31,893
- Bit Na. - Mom!

158
00:08:31,953 --> 00:08:34,293
Ji Seon, what's going on? You didn't even call.

159
00:08:34,723 --> 00:08:37,563
I have the day off, so I wanted to see Bit Na.

160
00:08:37,993 --> 00:08:41,163
I called Bit Na, but she didn't answer, so I came.

161
00:08:42,673 --> 00:08:45,873
I didn't know because at Great-grandfather's funeral,

162
00:08:45,943 --> 00:08:47,973
I was too busy dancing and having fun to hear it.

163
00:08:49,243 --> 00:08:53,613
- What? Dancing at a funeral? - Yes.

164
00:08:53,683 --> 00:08:56,613
It's a long story. Shall we go inside?

165
00:08:57,013 --> 00:08:58,613
Oh my, home?

166
00:08:58,953 --> 00:09:01,853
No one's home. They're all at Grandfather's funeral.

167
00:09:03,523 --> 00:09:04,793
Hello, Ji Seon.

168
00:09:05,593 --> 00:09:07,793
Oh, hello, Cho Rong.

169
00:09:08,563 --> 00:09:12,263
Bit Na, if you get bored later, come on over. We can play hopscotch.

170
00:09:12,363 --> 00:09:15,233
Auntie. Mom, let's hurry inside, okay?

171
00:09:15,673 --> 00:09:16,673
Okay.

172
00:09:24,713 --> 00:09:25,783
A living funeral?

173
00:09:26,013 --> 00:09:28,183
While Great-grandfather was still alive,

174
00:09:28,183 --> 00:09:30,153
he wanted to meet us all.

175
00:09:30,613 --> 00:09:33,423
And great-grandmother said I was really pretty too.

176
00:09:33,483 --> 00:09:35,623
Wow, that's great, Bit Na.

177
00:09:36,223 --> 00:09:38,993
Getting a Great-grandmother and a Great-grandfather.

178
00:09:39,423 --> 00:09:44,133
Oh, the drawing I made to show you, it's in Dad's room. I'll go get it.

179
00:09:44,363 --> 00:09:46,063
- Okay. - Yes.

180
00:09:52,303 --> 00:09:53,773
- Eun Hyung. - Yes?

181
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:54,843
I...

182
00:09:55,473 --> 00:09:59,543
- I took care of all the debt. - What? How?

183
00:10:00,083 --> 00:10:02,653
They caught the scammers, so I got some of it back,

184
00:10:02,913 --> 00:10:05,723
and I took out a loan from my company for the rest.

185
00:10:05,783 --> 00:10:07,383
I still had the loan we took out when we got married,

186
00:10:07,453 --> 00:10:08,623
so I didn't think it would be possible,

187
00:10:08,823 --> 00:10:12,123
but the employee loan limit just happened to go up last week.

188
00:10:12,723 --> 00:10:15,493
The interest rate is lower than a bank's,

189
00:10:16,063 --> 00:10:17,233
so I applied right away.

190
00:10:18,693 --> 00:10:21,533
That's great. I'm so relieved, Ji Seon. Really.

191
00:10:21,963 --> 00:10:24,373
Well, it's still a loan from the company,

192
00:10:24,933 --> 00:10:26,243
and debt is debt.

193
00:10:27,773 --> 00:10:28,813
Oh, right.

194
00:10:29,173 --> 00:10:31,973
That money you sent me yesterday, what was that for?

195
00:10:32,143 --> 00:10:34,943
From my academy teaching fees...

196
00:10:35,283 --> 00:10:36,513
and the money I saved from my part-time job,

197
00:10:36,583 --> 00:10:37,583
I sent you a little.

198
00:10:38,553 --> 00:10:39,823
It seemed like you were having such a hard time...

199
00:10:39,883 --> 00:10:40,883
paying off the debt by yourself.

200
00:10:41,183 --> 00:10:43,153
Why would you send me money, Eun Hyung?

201
00:10:44,223 --> 00:10:45,463
Because of me,

202
00:10:46,293 --> 00:10:47,863
you lost everything.

203
00:10:48,933 --> 00:10:50,593
That just makes me feel even worse.

204
00:10:50,663 --> 00:10:53,033
What are you talking about? Who lost everything?

205
00:10:53,263 --> 00:10:55,673
I have the greatest treasure of all, our Bit Na.

206
00:10:57,233 --> 00:10:58,503
So from now on,

207
00:10:59,503 --> 00:11:01,543
don't let yourself be so crushed by money,

208
00:11:02,043 --> 00:11:04,273
and take care of yourself too, okay?

209
00:11:08,313 --> 00:11:10,953
- Mom, look. - Okay.

210
00:11:12,053 --> 00:11:15,123
- Ta-da. - Wow, you're a great artist.

211
00:11:18,593 --> 00:11:20,423
Who's this here?

212
00:11:20,963 --> 00:11:23,533
Aunt Cho Rong. We went on a picnic together,

213
00:11:23,593 --> 00:11:26,103
ate delicious kimbap and mung bean pancakes,

214
00:11:26,163 --> 00:11:27,533
and played with bubbles.

215
00:11:28,263 --> 00:11:30,803
You all went on a picnic together?

216
00:11:31,003 --> 00:11:33,973
Right, Cho Rong planned it for Bit Na.

217
00:11:34,843 --> 00:11:37,973
Bit Na had so much fun that day, more than she had in a long time.

218
00:11:39,343 --> 00:11:40,413
I see.

219
00:11:41,543 --> 00:11:44,013
You seem to be very close with Cho Rong.

220
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:45,623
Of course, we're very close.

221
00:11:45,883 --> 00:11:47,853
We grew up together like brother and sister.

222
00:11:49,153 --> 00:11:51,293
You have no idea how much Cho Rong cares for Bit Na.

223
00:11:52,053 --> 00:11:54,023
She's such a kind and thoughtful person.

224
00:11:54,563 --> 00:11:55,593
Is that so?

225
00:11:57,263 --> 00:11:59,103
So the flowers from before...

226
00:11:59,163 --> 00:12:01,933
Mom, when are you coming to see me again?

227
00:12:02,503 --> 00:12:03,533
Well...

228
00:12:04,433 --> 00:12:06,603
Every time I have a day off,

229
00:12:07,203 --> 00:12:08,473
I'll be sure to come see you.

230
00:12:11,643 --> 00:12:12,843
Oh, my pretty girl.

231
00:12:14,713 --> 00:12:16,253
The Chairman will be okay, right?

232
00:12:17,183 --> 00:12:18,713
He'll be fine.

233
00:12:19,123 --> 00:12:21,053
I've lived at the Chairman's house since I was little,

234
00:12:21,053 --> 00:12:22,123
so I know him well.

235
00:12:22,393 --> 00:12:25,253
The Chairman has incredible mental fortitude.

236
00:12:26,923 --> 00:12:30,833
He'll pull through just fine. So please, trust me.

237
00:12:30,933 --> 00:12:31,933
Okay?

238
00:12:32,603 --> 00:12:34,233
The more I think about it, the more incredible it seems.

239
00:12:34,933 --> 00:12:38,373
He's my maternal grandfather, and your family has for a time...

240
00:12:38,433 --> 00:12:40,273
been like one big family with the Chairman's household.

241
00:12:40,573 --> 00:12:42,543
And my sister-in-law fell in love...

242
00:12:42,613 --> 00:12:44,843
with the Chairman's grandson at work.

243
00:12:46,613 --> 00:12:47,913
Doesn't it feel like a TV show?

244
00:12:48,213 --> 00:12:51,583
- A drama? - Yes. Three families, tangled up.

245
00:12:51,653 --> 00:12:53,323
Coincidence becomes inevitable, and finally, destiny.

246
00:12:54,053 --> 00:12:55,083
What if...

247
00:12:55,893 --> 00:12:57,223
there's a huge secret between the three families,

248
00:12:57,293 --> 00:13:00,363
- that we don't know about? - What?

249
00:13:00,623 --> 00:13:01,693
What kind of secret?

250
00:13:02,833 --> 00:13:03,863
So...

251
00:13:04,293 --> 00:13:07,233
The moment all the children fall in love,

252
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,973
a huge secret between the three families is revealed,

253
00:13:10,073 --> 00:13:11,733
and because of it, one family is completely shattered,

254
00:13:11,803 --> 00:13:13,373
the lovers are forced to break up,

255
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:16,513
and from that moment, a terrifying revenge begins.

256
00:13:16,973 --> 00:13:18,443
"I will destroy them."

257
00:13:19,683 --> 00:13:20,683
Writer.

258
00:13:21,743 --> 00:13:24,183
Yes. We were talking about our three families,

259
00:13:24,253 --> 00:13:25,253
but I think the conversation...

260
00:13:25,313 --> 00:13:26,653
has strayed into web novel territory...

261
00:13:27,953 --> 00:13:29,593
It's very interesting. Please continue.

262
00:13:30,753 --> 00:13:34,093
Did I? It must be an occupational hazard.

263
00:13:34,193 --> 00:13:36,333
Well, since you've caught the bug, let's just keep going with it.

264
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:38,233
So, in those families,

265
00:13:38,293 --> 00:13:40,263
couldn't there be a love story for the...

266
00:13:40,333 --> 00:13:42,603
youngest daughter and youngest son, like us?

267
00:13:42,703 --> 00:13:44,633
What? Like us?

268
00:13:45,843 --> 00:13:49,543
That depends on how you write it. It's just a novel, after all.

269
00:13:49,673 --> 00:13:52,343
Right? Go on, write one.

270
00:13:53,383 --> 00:13:56,913
I'm really looking forward to this. How their story will unfold.

271
00:13:58,283 --> 00:13:59,523
As for them...

272
00:14:00,383 --> 00:14:05,253
it's not exactly a love story, more like some chemistry?

273
00:14:05,493 --> 00:14:08,723
Hey, that's not right. If there's some chemistry,

274
00:14:08,793 --> 00:14:10,863
it obviously has to end in love.

275
00:14:11,493 --> 00:14:13,033
What, are you discriminating against them...

276
00:14:13,103 --> 00:14:14,163
because they're the youngest?

277
00:14:14,233 --> 00:14:16,073
The character relationships are complicated enough as it is.

278
00:14:16,133 --> 00:14:18,233
Isn't it too much for the youngest ones...

279
00:14:18,303 --> 00:14:20,943
- to fall in love too? - What's too much about it?

280
00:14:21,973 --> 00:14:24,073
The youngest son has probably already fallen.

281
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,813
Fallen into a fateful love.

282
00:14:30,483 --> 00:14:32,213
Destiny, my foot.

283
00:14:33,223 --> 00:14:34,883
Stop it and get back to work.

284
00:14:42,963 --> 00:14:45,133
I told you, you don't have to walk me home.

285
00:14:45,493 --> 00:14:47,603
You should go. You must be tired today.

286
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:49,533
No, I'm not tired at all.

287
00:14:50,203 --> 00:14:54,073
Walking you home is how I unwind. You didn't know that?

288
00:14:54,703 --> 00:14:57,873
- The Chairman will be okay, right? - Of course.

289
00:14:58,173 --> 00:15:00,683
He's overcome situations far worse than this.

290
00:15:01,383 --> 00:15:04,953
- He went in to sleep. Don't worry. - Okay.

291
00:15:05,823 --> 00:15:06,823
By the way,

292
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,623
- did something happen to Gyeol? - To Gyeol?

293
00:15:11,993 --> 00:15:15,763
- Why do you ask? - Overheard something at the event.

294
00:15:16,693 --> 00:15:19,263
That there was a call from the police station.

295
00:15:19,533 --> 00:15:20,863
What? The police station?

296
00:15:22,263 --> 00:15:24,003
Gyeol is the last person who'd get into trouble with the law,

297
00:15:24,273 --> 00:15:26,073
so he shouldn't have anything to do with a police station.

298
00:15:26,673 --> 00:15:27,673
Really?

299
00:15:28,973 --> 00:15:30,513
I must have misheard something.

300
00:15:31,143 --> 00:15:34,583
- I'll go in now. - Wait. Can't I come in with you?

301
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:35,913
Just for a glass of cold water.

302
00:15:36,413 --> 00:15:40,023
Some other time. My dad doesn't seem to be feeling well today.

303
00:15:40,153 --> 00:15:41,453
Oh, that's right.

304
00:15:41,823 --> 00:15:44,353
- Okay, you should head in. - Get home safe.

305
00:15:44,423 --> 00:15:45,423
Okay.

306
00:16:07,413 --> 00:16:08,443
Yes.

307
00:16:09,283 --> 00:16:11,253
Jeongbin Police Station, Traffic Investigation Unit?

308
00:16:12,883 --> 00:16:13,883
What?

309
00:16:14,383 --> 00:16:15,483
You found it?

310
00:16:16,653 --> 00:16:19,563
Jeongbin Police Station, Traffic Investigation Unit? Why?

311
00:16:26,403 --> 00:16:28,803
- Are you all right, Dad? - Yes, I'm fine.

312
00:16:29,433 --> 00:16:31,103
Did you finish cleaning everything up?

313
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:32,673
Yes, of course.

314
00:16:33,503 --> 00:16:34,673
You didn't seem to be feeling well.

315
00:16:34,673 --> 00:16:37,143
Why are you in your study instead of resting?

316
00:16:37,873 --> 00:16:39,043
I'm all right now.

317
00:16:39,613 --> 00:16:42,183
I wonder if the Chairman has calmed down.

318
00:16:42,913 --> 00:16:45,653
I think he's feeling better. They said he was going to sleep.

319
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:47,753
I see. That's a relief.

320
00:16:49,353 --> 00:16:50,353
Dad.

321
00:16:50,853 --> 00:16:54,623
Is something wrong again? You can tell me anything.

322
00:16:55,563 --> 00:16:57,063
You know that your daughter...

323
00:16:57,463 --> 00:16:59,663
will always be on your side, no matter what.

324
00:17:00,163 --> 00:17:01,533
I know. Thank you.

325
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:05,073
I'm just feeling a little under the weather.

326
00:17:05,133 --> 00:17:06,273
You should go get some rest.

327
00:17:07,773 --> 00:17:09,343
You worked very hard preparing for today.

328
00:17:09,673 --> 00:17:11,043
Don't worry about me.

329
00:17:11,713 --> 00:17:13,843
- Well, get some rest. - All right.

330
00:17:26,223 --> 00:17:27,293
Is this the police station?

331
00:17:27,963 --> 00:17:30,593
I'd like to know what the retention period...

332
00:17:30,663 --> 00:17:32,663
is for traffic accident records.

333
00:17:34,133 --> 00:17:35,163
Pardon?

334
00:17:36,373 --> 00:17:37,633
For a case from about 20 years ago,

335
00:17:37,903 --> 00:17:40,273
I'm wondering if it's possible to look up the accident report.

336
00:17:42,913 --> 00:17:44,043
I'm sorry, what was that?

337
00:17:45,613 --> 00:17:47,683
You're saying they were most likely destroyed?

338
00:17:50,753 --> 00:17:53,053
Really? I see.

339
00:17:54,223 --> 00:17:56,553
A certificate of traffic accident report.

340
00:17:56,953 --> 00:17:58,693
Yes, I understand.

341
00:18:00,723 --> 00:18:03,393
(Traffic Accident Facts)

342
00:18:03,993 --> 00:18:06,433
Father, are you sure you're okay?

343
00:18:07,803 --> 00:18:09,103
Why do you keep asking?

344
00:18:09,503 --> 00:18:10,603
Can't you tell just by looking at me?

345
00:18:11,273 --> 00:18:14,843
It's such a relief, Father. For a moment at the living funeral,

346
00:18:14,903 --> 00:18:16,713
I was worried it would turn into a real one.

347
00:18:18,413 --> 00:18:20,883
I was told that Dr. Kim is on his way.

348
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:22,753
Honestly, I told you I'm fine.

349
00:18:23,353 --> 00:18:24,713
Why did you call him?

350
00:18:26,223 --> 00:18:27,923
By the way,

351
00:18:27,923 --> 00:18:29,723
you said you had something to tell us?

352
00:18:29,793 --> 00:18:34,063
Yes. I was very pleased today.

353
00:18:35,563 --> 00:18:36,793
Even after I'm gone,

354
00:18:37,593 --> 00:18:39,703
I want you to continue to get along...

355
00:18:40,463 --> 00:18:42,433
and rely on one another,

356
00:18:43,073 --> 00:18:47,773
- just as you did today. - There you go again.

357
00:18:47,843 --> 00:18:51,173
Please stop talking about leaving, Father.

358
00:18:52,243 --> 00:18:54,643
And as the eldest,

359
00:18:55,343 --> 00:18:56,783
I'll do my best to lead everyone.

360
00:18:58,483 --> 00:19:00,883
Yes, Chairman. We'll take your words to heart.

361
00:19:01,253 --> 00:19:04,253
Good. I'm counting on you.

362
00:19:06,123 --> 00:19:07,163
Father.

363
00:19:07,923 --> 00:19:09,863
This is the gift I wanted to give you earlier.

364
00:19:10,693 --> 00:19:13,433
I think you felt awkward accepting it in front of everyone,

365
00:19:13,503 --> 00:19:16,103
but it's just us now, so it's okay, right?

366
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:20,243
She prepared it for you. Please accept it gladly.

367
00:19:21,573 --> 00:19:23,013
- Yes. - All right.

368
00:19:23,373 --> 00:19:24,373
Thank you.

369
00:19:25,173 --> 00:19:26,313
Father, you see...

370
00:19:26,383 --> 00:19:28,743
They say you're supposed to open a gift...

371
00:19:28,813 --> 00:19:30,253
right after you get it.

372
00:19:37,823 --> 00:19:40,793
When I looked in your safe the other day,

373
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:43,733
I was surprised to find that the safe of a conglomerate chairman...

374
00:19:43,833 --> 00:19:45,263
was empty, without a single gold bar.

375
00:19:45,463 --> 00:19:46,663
That's why I...

376
00:19:48,803 --> 00:19:52,633
Besides, turtles are a symbol of longevity.

377
00:19:53,743 --> 00:19:55,873
Yes, thank you.

378
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:00,143
By the way, Kang Yeon Ja.

379
00:20:00,743 --> 00:20:03,253
Wait, did you come empty-handed?

380
00:20:05,283 --> 00:20:08,523
- I was planning to give it later... - Oh my.

381
00:20:08,853 --> 00:20:10,253
Why later?

382
00:20:11,023 --> 00:20:14,163
- What kind of gift did you prepare? - That's right.

383
00:20:14,723 --> 00:20:16,693
If you brought a gift, you should give it to him now.

384
00:20:17,933 --> 00:20:21,703
- Should I? All right. - I told you not to bring a gift.

385
00:20:33,713 --> 00:20:37,213
I'm a little out of practice with my knitting,

386
00:20:38,083 --> 00:20:42,383
but I hope you'll wear these gloves this winter, and next winter,

387
00:20:43,093 --> 00:20:47,163
so that we can continue to have warm winters together.

388
00:20:47,893 --> 00:20:50,693
Who even wears hand-knitted gloves these days?

389
00:20:51,393 --> 00:20:52,433
They're very...

390
00:20:53,163 --> 00:20:54,763
warm and wonderful.

391
00:20:56,133 --> 00:20:57,673
I'll wear these gloves...

392
00:20:58,533 --> 00:20:59,603
this winter,

393
00:21:00,273 --> 00:21:01,843
and have a warm winter.

394
00:21:02,543 --> 00:21:06,913
By the way, didn't Gyeol and Eun Ae get home earlier?

395
00:21:07,113 --> 00:21:10,453
I think they went upstairs to their room. Should I go get them?

396
00:21:11,053 --> 00:21:12,053
Okay.

397
00:21:50,293 --> 00:21:53,423
Oh, why are you back alone? Weren't they in the room?

398
00:21:53,723 --> 00:21:54,793
No, they're there,

399
00:21:55,163 --> 00:21:58,663
but it seems Team Leader Ko was tired and fell asleep.

400
00:21:59,393 --> 00:22:01,733
My goodness. Those two are ridiculous.

401
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:04,873
They're sharing a room, in a house full of adults?

402
00:22:07,403 --> 00:22:08,403
We're here.

403
00:22:10,443 --> 00:22:12,243
How could you two do this?

404
00:22:12,643 --> 00:22:16,283
Sharing a room in broad daylight with all the adults here?

405
00:22:17,583 --> 00:22:18,953
Your mother is right about that.

406
00:22:19,983 --> 00:22:22,953
I mean, even if you two aren't related by blood,

407
00:22:23,053 --> 00:22:24,753
there are still social conventions.

408
00:22:25,453 --> 00:22:27,493
You two need to break up immediately.

409
00:22:27,823 --> 00:22:29,293
That's enough.

410
00:22:37,973 --> 00:22:40,343
Eun Ae and I love each other.

411
00:22:41,173 --> 00:22:43,543
Father, social conventions are important as you say,

412
00:22:44,943 --> 00:22:46,543
but we have no intention of breaking up.

413
00:22:47,113 --> 00:22:48,343
What? So what is this all about?

414
00:22:48,513 --> 00:22:51,383
Are you trying to ask for our permission to get married?

415
00:22:51,583 --> 00:22:53,583
We're not saying we want to get married right away,

416
00:22:54,653 --> 00:22:58,853
but we have promised to never let go of each other.

417
00:22:59,423 --> 00:23:02,063
Please give us your official blessing to date.

418
00:23:02,193 --> 00:23:04,963
Oh my goodness. This is ridiculous.

419
00:23:05,363 --> 00:23:09,303
- Our family is a complete mess. - Why is it ridiculous?

420
00:23:09,363 --> 00:23:11,633
The couple's happiness is more important...

421
00:23:11,703 --> 00:23:13,003
than what others think.

422
00:23:13,243 --> 00:23:15,773
The two of them are not related by blood at all.

423
00:23:17,243 --> 00:23:18,713
What are your thoughts?

424
00:23:19,813 --> 00:23:20,883
Oh, yes. Well,

425
00:23:20,943 --> 00:23:23,783
we don't see any major issues with it.

426
00:23:24,983 --> 00:23:27,553
Dr. Kim is here, Grandfather. I ran into him at the gate.

427
00:23:27,883 --> 00:23:29,553
Oh, welcome, Dr. Kim.

428
00:23:30,353 --> 00:23:33,963
- Sorry to make you come this way. - Not at all.

429
00:23:35,223 --> 00:23:37,663
Let's go inside, Chairman. I need to examine you.

430
00:23:37,733 --> 00:23:40,333
Goodness, I keep telling you I'm fine.

431
00:23:41,263 --> 00:23:44,403
We'll continue this conversation later.

432
00:23:45,003 --> 00:23:46,743
Everyone should head home for today.

433
00:23:47,673 --> 00:23:48,873
Thank you all for coming.

434
00:23:52,043 --> 00:23:53,443
We'll see you again. Okay?

435
00:23:54,113 --> 00:23:57,553
Let's talk again soon. All right?

436
00:24:03,193 --> 00:24:05,393
I'll say it one more time. It's absolutely not happening.

437
00:24:06,323 --> 00:24:07,623
There's a proper way to do things.

438
00:24:08,393 --> 00:24:09,423
The proper way?

439
00:24:09,763 --> 00:24:13,463
- What proper way is that? - Honey, that's enough. Let's go.

440
00:24:14,403 --> 00:24:16,973
Thank you for your time today. We will take our leave.

441
00:24:18,203 --> 00:24:22,303
- You two are coming with us, right? - Yes, Mom. We'll be going now.

442
00:24:23,373 --> 00:24:25,343
Get home safe. You too, Gyeol and Eun Ae.

443
00:24:25,343 --> 00:24:26,413
It's been a long day.

444
00:24:27,313 --> 00:24:28,313
Okay.

445
00:24:31,813 --> 00:24:34,323
Wait, what's with the mood? Did something happen?

446
00:24:35,023 --> 00:24:37,253
Gyeol asked for our blessing for the two of them.

447
00:24:37,253 --> 00:24:39,023
Can you believe that?

448
00:24:39,153 --> 00:24:41,223
I don't see why it's so out of the question.

449
00:24:42,263 --> 00:24:43,493
Well, I'm going upstairs.

450
00:24:43,863 --> 00:24:46,333
Oh my gosh, not him, too.

451
00:24:46,833 --> 00:24:50,533
Isn't this just ridiculous? I mean, they cannot have it all.

452
00:24:50,603 --> 00:24:52,603
The mother wants to be the daughter of this house,

453
00:24:52,873 --> 00:24:54,243
and her daughter wants to be the daughter-in-law.

454
00:24:54,543 --> 00:24:56,343
Do they think they can take every position for themselves?

455
00:24:57,013 --> 00:24:59,073
It might be different if they gave one of them up.

456
00:24:59,413 --> 00:25:00,743
Wait, easy there, Crystal.

457
00:25:01,513 --> 00:25:06,013
Wait. On second thought, what if we give Gyeol our blessing...

458
00:25:06,083 --> 00:25:08,523
on the condition that Kang Yeon Ja drops her claim?

459
00:25:11,853 --> 00:25:12,893
Oh my.

460
00:25:18,763 --> 00:25:20,363
What are you so deep in thought about?

461
00:25:23,003 --> 00:25:24,233
About the kids.

462
00:25:25,773 --> 00:25:28,803
We always thought we were fine with it,

463
00:25:29,343 --> 00:25:31,443
but it seems not everyone feels the same way.

464
00:25:31,873 --> 00:25:33,443
That is life.

465
00:25:33,443 --> 00:25:35,443
You cannot expect everyone to think the same.

466
00:25:36,983 --> 00:25:40,783
When I saw the two of them upstairs earlier today,

467
00:25:41,453 --> 00:25:43,123
they just looked so fond of each other.

468
00:25:44,723 --> 00:25:46,723
Team Leader Ko has been so lonely until now.

469
00:25:47,093 --> 00:25:48,923
I just do not want him to be lonely anymore.

470
00:25:51,593 --> 00:25:52,663
You go to sleep first.

471
00:25:52,663 --> 00:25:54,363
I am going to have a quick word with Eun Ae.

472
00:26:12,013 --> 00:26:13,653
(Rise In Night Intersection Crashes, Driver Caution Needed)

473
00:26:13,723 --> 00:26:15,383
(A Guide To Initial Response After A Traffic Accident)

474
00:26:15,453 --> 00:26:16,753
(Traffic Accident Compensation, What's The Payout?)

475
00:26:16,823 --> 00:26:18,993
(May 12, 2001: Car Overturns, Driver Rescued And Hospitalized)

476
00:26:20,993 --> 00:26:21,993
Yes, come in.

477
00:26:23,763 --> 00:26:26,333
- Oh, you're still awake? - Yes.

478
00:26:26,863 --> 00:26:27,933
What were you up to?

479
00:26:28,103 --> 00:26:30,873
Oh, I was just looking up an article.

480
00:26:32,373 --> 00:26:34,743
I heard something on my way up. Is Team Leader Ko okay?

481
00:26:35,003 --> 00:26:38,543
- It sounded like bad sleep-talking. - Oh, it's not that...

482
00:26:39,043 --> 00:26:41,883
He's been having nightmares every night.

483
00:26:42,283 --> 00:26:43,313
Nightmares about what?

484
00:26:43,453 --> 00:26:45,983
He keeps dreaming about the scene of the accident...

485
00:26:46,053 --> 00:26:47,153
where his father died.

486
00:26:47,453 --> 00:26:51,393
- An accident? What accident? - A car accident.

487
00:26:51,993 --> 00:26:56,063
His father died at the scene. He was the only survivor.

488
00:26:56,323 --> 00:26:58,363
What? A car accident?

489
00:26:58,533 --> 00:27:02,063
The trauma made him lose all his memories of the accident,

490
00:27:02,203 --> 00:27:05,433
but lately, it seems bits and pieces are coming back in his dreams.

491
00:27:06,603 --> 00:27:10,013
He even went to the police station to ask about the accident,

492
00:27:10,613 --> 00:27:12,273
but they just said the records from 25 years ago...

493
00:27:12,343 --> 00:27:13,343
had been discarded.

494
00:27:13,783 --> 00:27:14,783
Wait a second.

495
00:27:15,913 --> 00:27:17,713
Twenty-five years ago would be...

496
00:27:19,583 --> 00:27:20,583
In 2001?

497
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:23,693
Yes, when he was seven.

498
00:27:24,653 --> 00:27:25,793
What is it?

499
00:27:54,823 --> 00:27:57,693
(Our Happy Days)

500
00:27:57,823 --> 00:28:00,393
I could vaguely see what looked like an accident scene.

501
00:28:00,463 --> 00:28:03,023
There were people there. I want to see it more clearly.

502
00:28:04,363 --> 00:28:07,433
But I cannot remember anything. Father, do you happen to know?

503
00:28:07,703 --> 00:28:11,603
When I actually thought about being legally tied...

504
00:28:11,603 --> 00:28:13,303
to your mother on paper as family,

505
00:28:13,403 --> 00:28:16,043
it was actually kind of reassuring.

506
00:28:16,273 --> 00:28:18,413
But I have made up my mind now.

507
00:28:18,873 --> 00:28:21,983
Whatever you decide, just follow your heart.

508
00:28:27,253 --> 00:28:29,923
(Our Happy Days)
